# OPTIONAL, AND FOR DEVELOPMENT ONLY.
#
# Lyric Veil asks for your Spotify client ID in its settings panel on first run,
# and stores it in %APPDATA%\lyric-veil\config.json. That is the supported way
# to configure it, and the only way that works in a packaged build.
#
# Setting it here just skips the setup screen while running `npm run dev`, so you
# do not re-enter it on every restart. Packaged builds ignore this value on
# purpose: a client ID compiled into a public binary belongs to whoever built it,
# and Spotify only lets accounts on that app's allowlist sign in.
#
# Redirect URI to register on your Spotify app:
#   http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback
# Use 127.0.0.1, NOT localhost -- Spotify rejects localhost for new redirect URIs.
# Scopes needed: user-read-playback-state user-read-currently-playing
#
# There is no client secret. Authentication is Authorization Code + PKCE.
MAIN_VITE_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
